# DuetSoftwareFramework packages from a separately published build of our
# own, installed in place of the Duet3D archive's.
#
# One line per package:
#
#   <package> sha256:<checksum of the published .deb> <https location>
#
# The DSF packages pin each other to one exact version and check it again at
# runtime, so a build of our own is installed as a whole: every package that
# pkg/build.sh --packages=progs,dwc,meta produces in the fork, at a version
# <dsf.version>+<suffix> (3.7.0~rc.2+mp.1 for a modified 3.7.0~rc.2).
# duetwebcontrol is among them: the build packages our fork of Duet Web
# Control, Meltingplot/DuetWebControl, at a version of the same form, and the
# meta package pins it. duetsd and reprapfirmware come from the archive, where
# the build's meta package pins them; reprapfirmware at dsf.rrf_version, which
# the meta package has to accept. An empty list installs the archive's
# packages. Only a published build is taken, checked against the pin: no local
# path, no fallback, a mismatch stops the build. See "Installing a
# DuetSoftwareFramework build of our own" in the README.
#
# A board firmware file is not a package of the build; it goes through
# firmware.list.

# 3.7.0+mp.1: upstream v3.7-dev at 3.7.0, which no longer rejects the skip
# keyword outside G-code files and reads the layer count, the filament used,
# the generator and the print time from the headers of more slicers (the
# filters are in config.json, which the image puts over the printer's copy on
# every boot), plus our fix for a DCS crash on a non-finite expression result
# and our fix that keeps the patches coming for a model collection the
# firmware replaces, such as a board's drivers after an M999. The packages are
# built with root as owner of every file. Duet Web Control comes from our
# fork, 3.7.0+mp.1, the tag pkg/dwc-version in the fork pins: upstream 3.7.0
# with the CHX 350 operator interface, which leaves machine actions such as
# preheating, homing and filament change to the flow macros of the printer
# configuration, reports a flow as completed only when it reaches its
# `echo ";; Completed"` line, which it keeps out of the notifications, moves
# the axes while a job is paused and shows history and analysis from the
# QualityAssurance plugin. The release of that Duet Web Control also carries
# the interface's SBC backend, which plugins.list pins at the same version.
# Duet3D has not published 3.7.0 yet, so the meta package still accepts the
# firmware of 3.7.0-rc.1 (pkg/firmware-version in the fork), which
# dsf.rrf_version installs. Earlier builds: mp.9 of 3.7.0-rc.2 brought the
# root ownership, mp.8 the object model fix, packaged as the build user
# (1001), mp.7 carried Duet Web Control 3.7.0-rc.2+mp.6 and the object model
# changes of upstream, mp.6 3.7.0-rc.2+mp.5, mp.5 3.7.0-rc.2+mp.4, mp.4
# 3.7.0-rc.2+mp.3, mp.3 3.7.0-rc.2+mp.2, mp.9 of 3.7.0-rc.1 brought remote
# sensors on CAN expansion boards, mp.8 checked N line numbers in job and
# macro files, mp.7 RRF-style checksums on numbered lines, mp.6 kept the
# object model in step after an SPI transfer timeout.
